			<div class="content" id="post-content-1885105">
									

<p>Neutral vote for now.</p>
<p>At first, I really liked this skip.</p>
<p>Then I read the tale.</p>
<p>I REALLY loved the tale and upvoted it. But there is really nothing in this skip that's not also in the tale. One is a clinical article that's a small window of what we see in the tale. The tale tells us what's really going on. And believe me, I think its its a great, wonderful idea but I'm not giving you multiple upvotes for the same idea. This needs something more, a bit more of a hook, something new that the Foundation knows about it that we didn't already get from &quot;The Worm.&quot;</p>
<p>EDIT: Also, you tried to tie this to SCP-882, didn't you? This bit here: &quot; The assembly has suffered extensive damage, with evidence that a large section (approximately 12 cubic meters) has been violently removed. &quot; That's the same size as SCP-882 (post recovery).</p>

